# Release documentation (nextDash)

When the user asks to document a release (e.g. `v2026.07.26`):

## 1. What's new modal + config Overview

- Add `static/data/whats-new/v<TAG>.json` with `tag`, `date`, `releasedAt`, `modalLead`, and `sections[]` (`badge`: `new` | `fix`, `text` HTML).
- Prepend the entry to `static/data/whats-new/index.json` (newest first).
- **Config → Overview → Latest update** reads `index.json[0]` and that file's `modalLead` — no separate overview copy; keep `modalLead` suitable as a plain-text summary (HTML is stripped in the overview panel).

## 2. Cache-bust tokens

- Bump together in `static/js/whats-new-stub.js`:
  - `DASHBOARD_RELEASE` → `2026.07-dashboard-release-vNNN` (+1)
  - `NEXTDASH_WHATS_NEW_DATA_VERSION` → `whats-new-vNNN` (+1)

## 3. CHANGELOG.md

- Add TOC link and full section after `## Unreleased` (same style: lead paragraph, ### New / Fixes / Docs, file references where useful).
- Leave `## Unreleased` as "Nothing yet."

## 4. README.md & MANUAL.md

- Update feature lists, version examples (e.g. analytics release tag), and manual sections for user-visible changes only.

## 5. Config → Help → What's new recap

- Prepend a `<li>` to `helpPageWhatsNewItems` in **all four** locale files: `locales/en.json`, `nl.json`, `de.json`, `fr.json`.
- Mention that Overview summarises the same release when relevant.

## 6. Verify

- `npm run validate:json` (or parse JSON files)
- `go test ./...` (especially `release_version_test.go`)
- Optional: Playwright `tests/config-overview.spec.js` (release tag visible)

## Do not commit unless the user explicitly asks.
